When a canvas gets its first drawing, Ladybird updates what it records
for the canvas right away, so a recording that follows in the same task
draws it. The other engines do the same bookkeeping as each drawing
call is made: Gecko’s CanvasRenderingContext2D::FillRect() calls
RedrawUser(), WebKit’s CanvasRenderingContext2DBase::fillRect() calls
willUpdateEntireContents(), and Blink’s CanvasRenderingContext2D::
WillDraw() calls CanvasRenderingContext::DidDraw(). None of them waits
for the next frame to present the pixels for that.
